From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Taozuhong <taozuhong@hotmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 02:43:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] MinGW: libpas/bmalloc and compatibility shims

Compatibility shims:
- err.h shim for the GLib/unix code paths that use err()/errx();
- unifdef format fixes (eval%ld for LP64).
- pas_utils.h/err.h format attributes mapped per mingw-w64 stdio.h
  (MinGW gcc -> __gnu_printf__, clang/host unchanged).

libpas/bmalloc:
- pas_thread.h: drop the MSVC pthread emulation in favour of the
  system <pthread.h> under MinGW; exclude the emulation .c; guard
  scavenger/status_reporter thread main signatures.
- Explicit <windows.h> includes for PAS_OS(WINDOWS) files that use
  WinAPI without any Windows header (upstream relies on prefix
  headers): pas_committed_pages_vector.c, pas_page_malloc.c,
  pas_scavenger.c, pas_probabilistic_guard_malloc_allocator.c,
  pas_lock.c (futex WaitOnAddress/INFINITE - mingw-w64 synchapi.h
  does not pull winbase.h), pas_status_reporter.c (Sleep).
- __PAS_API expands to nothing under __MINGW32__: PE/COFF has no
  visibility semantics and MinGW GCC warns on every annotated
  declaration; libpas links as a static library.
- pas_large_sharing_pool.h: keep [[clang::preferred_type]] only
  under __clang__ (GCC ignores it on PE and warns per TU).
- bmalloc/CMakeLists.txt: link synchronization on MINGW
  (WaitOnAddress/WakeByAddress* live in libsynchronization.a);
  bmalloc is static so the requirement propagates to the final
  JavaScriptCore link.
